# release: the flow of depot yardr's releases. A release bead is one version,
# titled "yardr vX.Y.Z": build tags the base and waits for the draft CI
# makes for the tag, mckean signs the draft's checksums by hand, verify
# checks the signature and each archive's attestation, and publish releases
# the draft and files the yardr.dev sync bead. The script the exec group
# runs is contrib/release/stage; docs/install.md "Making a release" says
# how a release is cut with the yard. A failed verify asks for the
# signature again; anything else failed or questioned waits in decide for a
# person, who advances it to the stage it should retry.
backlog -> build
build -> sign on done | decide on failed | decide on question
sign -> verify on done
verify -> publish on done | sign on failed | decide on question
publish -> published on done | decide on failed | decide on question
decide -> backlog | build | sign | verify | publish
published terminal
